@@ -0,0 +1,13 @@
+## Context
+
+`src/patch.ts` has `applyPatch` and a private JSON `equal` (key-order independent). Members are set safely with `Object.defineProperty`, so `__proto__` is plain data.
+
+## Decisions
+
+- New `src/diff.ts`, recursive diff, re-exported from `src/index.ts`. Export `equal` from `src/patch.ts` (not from `index.ts`) to share one definition of JSON equality.
+- Objects: for each key only in `from`, `remove`; for each key only in `to`, `add`; for common keys, recurse. Use `Object.hasOwn`/`Object.keys` so `__proto__` works.
+- Arrays: trim the common prefix and suffix, then diff the overlapping middle element by element (recursing), then `remove` surplus `from` elements at the same index (repeated) or `add` surplus `to` elements in ascending order. A single middle insertion/removal thus yields one operation.
+- Type mismatch or differing scalars: `replace`. Arrays and objects are distinct types.
+- Values in `add`/`replace` are `structuredClone`d; inputs are never mutated.
+- Ops within an array are emitted so indices remain valid: in-place edits first, then removals/additions at the tail of the changed window.
+- Not generating `move`/`copy`/`test`: minimal-size optimisation is out of scope; the patch is correct and localized.
